<!-- WHAT IS THE DASHBOARD -->

<section class="section">

    <div class="section-label">
        DASHBOARD INTELLIGENCE
    </div>

    <h2>
        What Is The Dashboard?
    </h2>

    <p>
        The dashboard is not designed to predict outcomes.
        It is designed to provide visibility into a live execution cycle.
    </p>

    <p>
        Every panel represents a component of the operational structure.
        The objective is to understand how execution progresses from positioning to completion.
    </p>

</section>

<!-- EXECUTION STAGE -->

<section class="section">

    <h2>
        Execution Stage
    </h2>

    <p>
        Execution Stage shows the current location of the cycle.
        Think of it as a marker on a journey.
    </p>

    <p>
        As stages advance:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>Positioning expands</li>
        <li>Exposure develops</li>
        <li>Progression grows</li>
        <li>Completion approaches</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        The stage tells you where the system currently stands.
    </p>

</section>

<!-- PROGRESSION LEVEL -->

<section class="section">

    <h2>
        Progression Level
    </h2>

    <p>
        Progression Level tracks advancement through the cycle.
    </p>

    <p>
        This section helps observers understand movement.
    </p>

    <p>
        A higher progression level does not guarantee a result.
        It simply indicates that the cycle has advanced further through its predefined structure.
    </p>

</section>

<!-- CAPITAL DEPLOYED -->

<section class="section">

    <h2>
        Capital Deployed
    </h2>

    <p>
        Capital Deployed measures the amount currently allocated within the cycle.
    </p>

    <p>
        This allows observers to see:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>Current commitment</li>
        <li>Exposure growth</li>
        <li>Deployment scaling</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        The objective is visibility, not prediction.
    </p>

</section>

<!-- REMAINING CAPACITY -->

<section class="section">

    <h2>
        Remaining Capacity
    </h2>

    <p>
        Remaining Capacity shows how much operational room still exists inside the cycle.
    </p>

    <p>
        This section answers:
    </p>

    <blockquote>
        How much structure remains available?
    </blockquote>

    <p>
        Many observers focus only on what has been deployed.
        Experienced operators also watch what remains.
    </p>

</section>

<!-- SYSTEM SUMMARY -->

<section class="section">

    <h2>
        System Summary
    </h2>

    <p>
        The System Summary acts as the cycle's intelligence report.
    </p>

    <p>
        It consolidates:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>Stage Position</li>
        <li>Progression Level</li>
        <li>Capital Deployed</li>
        <li>Projected Returns</li>
        <li>Current Status</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        This section provides the clearest snapshot of the cycle.
    </p>

</section>

<!-- CYCLE RESET LOGIC -->

<section class="section">

    <h2>
        Cycle Reset Logic
    </h2>

    <p>
        Every cycle eventually ends.
    </p>

    <p>
        The dashboard continuously prepares for that transition.
    </p>

    <p>
        Reset logic tracks:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>Future cycle preparation</li>
        <li>Structure continuity</li>
        <li>Operational progression</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        Completion is not the end.
        Completion creates the starting point for the next cycle.
    </p>

</section>

